      <h1>How to Build an APK on Android</h1>
      <p class="lead">Compile standard Android projects into installable APKs right from your phone.</p>
      <h2>1. Install OpenBuild IDE &amp; Toolchains</h2>
      <p>Install the <a href="/download">v0.1.0 APK</a> and verify JDK, Gradle, and Android Build Tools paths.</p>
      <h2>2. Create or Open a Project</h2>
      <p>Ensure <code>AndroidManifest.xml</code>, <code>build.gradle</code>, and your Java/XML files are in place.</p>
      <h2>3. Run Gradle &amp; Retrieve the APK</h2>
      <p>Execute your debug build task, inspect the build output log, and locate <code>app-debug.apk</code> in your build outputs folder.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
